  data:  # bdbe
    kind: work_item  # bdbe
    title: "pub/sub name resolution stops at the file: imported constants, Class.ATTR constants and function-local constants stay unresolved"  # bdbe
    status: todo_hard  # bdbe
    priority: 3  # bdbe
    parent:  # bdbe
    tags:  # bdbe
    - protocol_linkers  # bdbe
    - analysis_quality  # bdbe
    isbefore: []  # bdbe
    duplicate_of: []  # bdbe
    not_duplicate_of: []  # bdbe
    pr_ref:  # bdbe
    description: "**Gap left by WI-misod-toruv-gimip-botuj-kadup-ludon-damib-buguk.** The shared `linkers/_name_args.py` `ConstantResolver` resolves a pub/sub topic / channel / event identifier only to a SAME-FILE, MODULE-SCOPE string constant. Three common shapes stay `unresolved` (value None, `variable_match` identifier join at 0.65):\n\n1. an imported constant: `from settings import ORDERS_TOPIC` / `import { OPEN_CHANNEL } from './channels'`;\n2. a class or object attribute: `Topics.ORDERS`, `config.topic`, `EVENTS.USER_CREATED`, Java `KafkaTopics.ORDERS`;\n3. a function-local constant (`const CH = 'x'` inside a function).\n\nFor (1) an imported constant used by a publisher and a LITERAL used by its subscriber still miss each other: the identifier join cannot reach a string, by design. A cure would follow the import to the defining file's module constants (the import graph is available after analysis) and resolve `Class.ATTR` against same-repo class-level string constants, keeping the \"any other binding leaves it unresolved\" rule.\n\n**Measure first:** WI-misod's A/B gives per-repo counts of `unresolved` sites (see its discussion note); how many of those are shapes 1-3 vs genuinely dynamic values (env lookups, parameters) is NOT measured."  # bdbe
    fields: {}  # bdbe
